---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import About from "../components/About.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<Base
  title="ve"
  description="Viscoelastic earthquake cycles from boundary elements alone: postseismic motion, the cycle of a locked fault, afterslip and a subducting slab, with no volume mesh."
  current="home"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <h1>ve<span class="sub">viscoelastic earthquake cycles, boundary elements only</span></h1>
    <About />
  </Fragment>

  <div
    id="hero"
    class="hero"
    aria-label="The free surface above a megathrust, coloured by how far it has moved vertically since the earthquake and displaced by that motion, looping from the earthquake to one hundred relaxation times"
  ></div>
  <p class="cap">
    The ground above a megathrust, from the earthquake to 100 Maxwell times
    after it. Colour is the <b>vertical displacement since the earthquake</b>
    (red up, blue down), and the surface is displaced by that motion,
    exaggerated. The fault (<b>pink</b>) dips 20&deg; through a 30&nbsp;km
    elastic plate into a Maxwell substrate; the rupture is 300&nbsp;km long.
    The sheet below the surface is the base of the plate. The model has 219,315
    unknowns, all of them on boundaries, and was solved fourteen times, once
    per Laplace state. Drag to orbit. See
    <a href={`${base}concepts/`}>Concepts</a> for how fourteen elastic solves
    become every time, and <a href={`${base}examples/`}>Examples</a> to move
    the clock yourself.
  </p>

  <style>
    .hero { position: relative; min-height: 440px; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; cursor: grab; }
    .hero:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  </style>
  <style is:global>
    .hero canvas { display: block; }
    .hero .clock {
      position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 4px; font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--fg-dim); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
  </style>
  <script>
    import { startHero } from "../viz/hero";
    startHero(document.getElementById("hero")!, import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
  </script>
</Base>
